<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_*   CathedralPass - CATHEDRAL_MISSION_BOON_OFFERS_1 (arc spec §1 stage 1, §3 bullet 3)

  The first favours. Once the clan is TOLERATED, missions against what the Assailant left behind (the
  self-replicating rot of 03_deep_history.md §The Assailant) reach the clan through the two deniable
  channels the spec names: a Free Droid enclave runner, or the Utinni herself. Nothing in any string ties them
  to the Cathedral, names an asker, or says what a mission is for; the player only notices, afterwards, that the
  ground has been easier. Every string here passes cathedral_arc_lint.py at stage 1 and at -1 (the linter also
  forbids the word "Assailant" in player text: it is §GM truth).

  SIX REQUESTS, ONE SHAPE: three per channel, so a request is not read word for word again for about six weeks of
  play. Each channel's abstract parent carries the whole quest (root) and its arrival and success letters; a child
  carries only its own name and description. The GM blackboard offers them in this file's order (channels
  alternate).

  SHAPE (one, shared by both channels): accept, and a pack of animals gone wrong walks in (vanilla
  QuestNode_ManhunterPack, the same incident the Royalty threat quests use); kill as many of that race as the pack
  holds (vanilla QuestNode_PawnsKilled, the Decree_Hunt node) and the mission ends in Success. If too few of
  that race are left alive to finish it, it fails; so does losing the map. No asker, no faction, no reward roll:
  what a completed mission earns is Regard, which the blackboard reads from the ended quest (EndedSuccess, root
  defName RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_*) and never Imperial Heat (K2). Fallback text is the whole text: the
  Oracle, if present, may only revoice it.

  TRIGGER: rootSelectionWeight 0 (never rolled); fired only by the paired RUT_GiveQuest_CathedralAssailantMission_*
  incidents (baseChance 0) when the GM blackboard offers them. RUT_QuestNode_GetRaceOfKind is this mod's one
  custom node (Source/CathedralFavours.cs): a SlateRef cannot read $animalKindDef.race.
-->
<Defs>

  <QuestScriptDef Abstract="True" Name="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionBase">
    <rootSelectionWeight>0</rootSelectionWeight>
    <rootMinPoints>0</rootMinPoints>
    <defaultChallengeRating>2</defaultChallengeRating>
    <expireDaysRange>3~4</expireDaysRange>
    <everAcceptableInSpace>false</everAcceptableInSpace>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <!-- The enclave channel: a Free Droid relay that will not say who asked. -->
  <QuestScriptDef Abstract="True" Name="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionEnclave" ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionBase">
    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap" />
        <li Class="QuestNode_QuestUnique">
          <tag>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission</tag>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_ManhunterPack">
          <tag>blightedPack</tag>
          <customLetterLabel TKey="LetterLabelRUTEnclaveCullArrived">The pack the enclaves warned of</customLetterLabel>
          <customLetterText TKey="LetterTextRUTEnclaveCullArrived">The animals the enclaves warned of are here. They move wrong, too stiff in the shoulders and too quick to turn, and they are coming straight for the colony.</customLetterText>
        </li>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.RUT_QuestNode_GetRaceOfKind">
          <kind>$animalKindDef</kind>
          <storeAs>blightedRace</storeAs>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_PawnsKilled">
          <race>$blightedRace</race>
          <count>$animalCount</count>
          <outSignalPawnsNotAvailable>PackNotAvailable</outSignalPawnsNotAvailable>
          <node Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
            <nodes>
              <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
                <label TKey="LetterLabelRUTEnclaveCullDone">The pack is down</label>
                <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
                <text TKey="LetterTextRUTEnclaveCullDone">The last of them is dead. Burn what is left of them before it starts to spread.\n\nNobody from the enclaves comes to thank you. But the next time the crews work the plates out past the old works, the ground seems a little easier under them, and nobody can say why.</text>
              </li>
              <li Class="QuestNode_End">
                <outcome>Success</outcome>
              </li>
            </nodes>
          </node>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>PackNotAvailable</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>map.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>
      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <!-- The Utinni channel: the ship insists, and will not say how she knew. -->
  <QuestScriptDef Abstract="True" Name="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionUtinni" ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionBase">
    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap" />
        <li Class="QuestNode_QuestUnique">
          <tag>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission</tag>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_ManhunterPack">
          <tag>blightedPack</tag>
          <customLetterLabel TKey="LetterLabelRUTUtinniCullArrived">The pack on the screens</customLetterLabel>
          <customLetterText TKey="LetterTextRUTUtinniCullArrived">The pack the Utinni tracked has reached the colony. Up close the rot shows in how they run: as if each of them had been put together from two animals that never agreed.</customLetterText>
        </li>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.RUT_QuestNode_GetRaceOfKind">
          <kind>$animalKindDef</kind>
          <storeAs>blightedRace</storeAs>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_PawnsKilled">
          <race>$blightedRace</race>
          <count>$animalCount</count>
          <outSignalPawnsNotAvailable>PackNotAvailable</outSignalPawnsNotAvailable>
          <node Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
            <nodes>
              <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
                <label TKey="LetterLabelRUTUtinniCullDone">The screens go quiet</label>
                <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
                <text TKey="LetterTextRUTUtinniCullDone">The pack is dead and the Utinni clears her screens without a word.\n\nThat night the drone from the old works runs low and even, the calmest anyone has heard it.</text>
              </li>
              <li Class="QuestNode_End">
                <outcome>Success</outcome>
              </li>
            </nodes>
          </node>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>PackNotAvailable</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>map.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>
      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionEnclave">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_EnclaveRunner</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->A request from the enclaves</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->A Free Droid runner came in at dusk with a request it had plainly been made to learn word for word. The animals that range out past the old works have gone wrong, the way things go wrong near the breached vaults, and the enclaves want them put down before the rot in them spreads.\n\nThe runner would not say who asked the enclaves. It did not wait for an answer.\n\nAccept, and the pack will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionUtinni">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_UtinniInsists</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->The Utinni insists</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->The Utinni will not let it go. For three nights her receivers have followed something moving out past the old works, and this morning she put it on every screen aboard: a pack of animals gone wrong, with the same rot in them that there is in the breached vaults. She wants them dead before they get any closer.\n\nShe will not say how she knew where to look.\n\nAccept, and they will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionEnclave">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_EnclaveShrineRoad</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->The shrine-road</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->The enclave droids who keep the shrine-road sent word ahead of their next pilgrimage. A pack of animals has gone wrong in the dunes past the old works, sick with the same rot that seeps out of the breached vaults, and the road is not safe while they are on it.\n\nThey ask the clan to clear it. They do not say why it has to be the clan.\n\nAccept, and the pack will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionUtinni">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_UtinniFrequency</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->A frequency nobody uses</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->Something the Utinni hears on a frequency nobody else uses has her restless. She has marked a place out past the old works where a pack of animals has gone wrong, and she will not stop asking until they are dead.\n\nAsk her how she knows, and she changes the subject.\n\nAccept, and they will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionEnclave">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_EnclaveBeacon</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->A beacon in the night</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->An enclave beacon lit up on the ship's board overnight, repeating one short request in trade-cant until the deck crew answered it: animals gone wrong out past the old works, the rot in their blood, close enough now to smell. The enclaves have no fighters to send.\n\nNobody at the enclave could say who had asked them to pass the request on.\n\nAccept, and the pack will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_CathedralAssailantMissionUtinni">
    <defName>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_UtinniRestless</defName>
    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->The Utinni will not rest</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>
    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->For the third morning running the Utinni has woken the crew early with the same picture on every screen: a pack of animals gone wrong, the rot from the vaults in them, ranging nearer the ship each day. She is not frightened of them. She is impatient.\n\nShe has not said what she is impatient for.\n\nAccept, and they will come to you. Kill every one of them.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>
  </QuestScriptDef>

</Defs>
